1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,972
It's boiling in your room, so you open the window. But it's just as hot outside.

2
00:00:05,322 --> 00:00:09,973
So you stick a fan in the window. Okay, there's a breeze... but it's still hot air.

3
00:00:10,323 --> 00:00:14,355
Put some ice in front of the fan, and finally, the air feels cool.

4
00:00:14,705 --> 00:00:19,825
Then the ice melts, water spills everywhere, and you're back to a hot room... with a wet floor.

5
00:00:20,175 --> 00:00:23,993
We need ice that never runs out. So let's build our own ice.

6
00:00:24,343 --> 00:00:30,871
Start with a copper coil and fill it with a special liquid. It soaks up the heat from the air and turns into gas.

7
00:00:31,221 --> 00:00:33,461
Boom, our ice: the evaporator.

8
00:00:33,811 --> 00:00:43,091
But now that gas is full of heat, and it's 35 degrees outside. Heat only flows from hot to cold, so our gas has to be even hotter than outside.

9
00:00:43,441 --> 00:00:47,132
So let's squeeze it with a pump. Squeeze a gas, and it heats up.

10
00:00:47,482 --> 00:00:48,762
Meet the compressor.

11
00:00:49,112 --> 00:00:54,659
Now this super-hot gas has to lose its heat somewhere. So let's add a second coil outside.

12
00:00:55,009 --> 00:00:58,870
A fan blows the heat away, and the gas cools back into liquid.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:00,479
That's the condenser.

14
00:01:00,829 --> 00:01:05,394
But wait, this liquid is still warm and squeezed tight. It can't grab heat yet.

15
00:01:05,744 --> 00:01:12,464
So, one last trick: a tiny valve. The pressure drops, the liquid turns ice cold, and it heads back inside.

16
00:01:12,814 --> 00:01:19,171
Our ice that never melts! But a cold coil pulls water out of the air, just like a cold glass gets wet.

17
00:01:19,521 --> 00:01:23,681
So let's give it a small pipe to drip outside. No wet floor this time.

18
00:01:24,031 --> 00:01:28,938
But now it just keeps cooling, forever. Too cold, and a huge electricity bill.

19
00:01:29,288 --> 00:01:35,155
So let's give it a brain: a thermostat. When the room hits your temperature, the compressor takes a break.

20
00:01:35,505 --> 00:01:43,995
And all that room air brings dust. It sticks to the wet coil, blocks the air, and the AC gets weaker. So let's put a filter in front to catch it.

21
00:01:44,345 --> 00:01:49,295
Only one room is cool? Add some pipes in the ceiling to carry the cold air everywhere...

22
00:01:49,645 --> 00:01:51,415
...and you just built an AC.
